cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this inventory in academic work, please cite it. The data is a
  curated reading of a field, not a systematic review - cite it as a dataset
  you consulted, and check any individual classification against the paper
  itself before relying on it.
title: AI Security Research Inventory
abstract: >-
  A living inventory of AI-security research: 169 papers mapped across a
  41-category taxonomy, 386 measured overlaps between them, 8 documented open
  gaps, 7 security frameworks scored on their weakest mapped category, and the
  stated security priorities of 28 organisations. Published as a static
  dashboard and re-scanned weekly by a scheduled agent that classifies new work
  from peer-reviewed venues and frontier labs. Demand scores are editorial
  estimates of visible investment, not measurements; the published methodology
  names six biases they carry.
type: dataset
authors:
